WEBVTT

00:11:28.296 --> 00:11:31.926
And once I got interested in that,
I got interested in the study of evolution

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:33.605
as based in botanical exploration.

00:11:33.629 --> 00:11:37.204
Then I was really interested in the fact
that for a lot of the 19th century,

00:11:37.228 --> 00:11:39.776
the only science that women
could practice was botany,

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:42.548
because it was considered
kind of a lady sport,

00:11:42.572 --> 00:11:45.543
because women have traditionally
been the ones who grow things.

00:11:45.567 --> 00:11:47.674
So it was as though
botany was this back door

00:11:47.698 --> 00:11:50.250
that women could sneak into
into the scientific world,

00:11:50.274 --> 00:11:52.496
and they could have respect
and publish papers,

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:55.392
and they were basically
allowed to almost be full scientists.

00:11:55.416 --> 00:11:57.089
And I was like, that's interesting,

00:11:57.113 --> 00:11:59.069
and I started looking at all those women.

00:11:59.093 --> 00:12:02.516
And then the next thing you know,
I'm traveling to Tahiti and to Europe